# Service types for Motorola HALs that stock declares in VINTF but whose stock
# SELinux types do not exist in our policy. Defining our own is deliberate:
# copying stock's types verbatim does not work (stock registers ISensorExt under
# hal_graphics_composer_service, and AOSP's
# hal_attribute_service(hal_graphics_composer, ...) neverallow rejects granting
# hal_sensors_default `find` on it -- the policy will not build).
type vendor_hal_sensorext_service, service_manager_type;
type vendor_hal_arcsoftpp_service, service_manager_type;

# The three Motorola fingerprint extension interfaces the FPC HAL publishes
# alongside AOSP's IFingerprint. See hal_fingerprint_default.te and
# service_contexts. A type of our own for the same reason as the two above:
# stock's vendor_hal_fingerprint_fpc_service does not exist in this policy.
type vendor_hal_motofingerprint_service, service_manager_type;

# motorola.hardware.camera.desktop::ICameraDesktop -- the HIDL interface the
# camera provider probes for the desktop/DisplayPort camera path. It has no
# entry in any hwservice_contexts, so the lookup lands on
# default_android_hwservice, which no vendor domain may find:
#
#   avc: denied { find } for interface=motorola.hardware.camera.desktop::ICameraDesktop
#        sid=u:r:hal_camera_default:s0 scontext=u:r:hal_camera_default:s0
#        tcontext=u:object_r:default_android_hwservice:s0 tclass=hwservice_manager
#
# Nothing in this ROM implements the interface, so the lookup will still return
# null -- which is the answer the provider already handles. This only replaces
# a denial with a clean "not registered".
type vendor_hal_camera_desktop_hwservice, hwservice_manager_type;

# The two Motorola wireless-charging AIDL services. Stock's own type names are
# hal_motpowershare_aidl_service and hal_motwlc_aidl_service; neither exists in
# AOSP or in sepolicy_vndr, so as with the four types above they are declared
# here under a vendor_ prefix that makes their provenance obvious. Unlike
# ISensorExt there is no neverallow forcing the rename -- it is only for
# consistency with the rest of this file. See hal_motpowershare_default.te.
type vendor_hal_motpowershare_service, service_manager_type;
type vendor_hal_motwlc_service, service_manager_type;
